        "@value": "The field specifies the amount of energy consumed when training the AI model\nthat is being used in the AI system."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/AI/informationAboutTraining",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Information about different steps of the training process."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/AI/"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "informationAboutTraining"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range": [
      {
        "@id": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Information about different steps of the training process."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A detailed explanation of the training process,\nincluding the specific techniques, algorithms, and methods employed.\n\nExamples include:\n\n- training data used to train the AI model, along with any relevant details\n  about its source, quality, and pre-processing steps;\n- specific training algorithms employed, including stochastic gradient descent,\n  backpropagation, and reinforcement learning;\n- specific training techniques used to improve the performance or accuracy\n  of the AI model, such as transfer learning, fine-tuning, or active learning;\n  and\n- any evaluation metrics used to assess the performance of the AI model\n  during the training process, including accuracy, precision, recall, and F1\n  score."
      }
    ]
  },
